A core in user mode is not interrupted when another core changes its run queue or its turn, unless its timer is far.
A thread with time made ready there would wait behind a turn on spare time, or one due later, for that core's next tick.

Caught-by: fuzz-smp2
Report: a turn on spare time runs while a thread with time waits
Witness: fuzz-smp2 cores-join-interrupts

diff --git a/kernel/core.c b/kernel/core.c
--- a/kernel/core.c
+++ b/kernel/core.c
@@ -240,7 +240,7 @@ void core_notify(struct core *c)
      */
     if (c != core_self() &&
         (c->turn == NULL || (__atomic_load_n(&c->in_user, __ATOMIC_ACQUIRE) &&
-                             (c->wake_tick - c->ticks > 1 || (c->run_queue != 0 && c->run_stale))))) {
+                             (c->wake_tick - c->ticks > 1)))) {
         c->interrupt_owed = true;
     }
 #else
